// rod_bundle_channel_fixedB_gas.prm   (GENERATED by gen_rod_bundle_channel_test_prm.py -- edit the generator, not this file)
// [Claude, 2026-09-21] LOCAL bundle-channel test: three mutually touching PARALLEL rods (gap -0.030 LU, r=3, L=18) = the bundle at the crash site of job 4252482, dragged through still water with the constant velocity
// (1e-09, 0.0, 0.0); axis (-0.743, 0.652, -0.151); domain 48x36x48 periodic in X and Y, water surface at z=34, 3x3x1 blocks of 16x12x48 (9 MPI ranks); centroid start (15.50,11.37,20.10).
// Production unit system (omega 1.99753, g 5.8258e-5, sigma 1.63945e-3); fluid sweep at |u|>0.17 + dense NaN scan armed from step 0. Everything else as in prms/hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidoff_2node_gjk_sanity_18k_gas.prm.
// hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidoff_2node_gjk_sanity_18k_gas.prm   (copy of ..._frontblock_pidon_2node_gjk_sanity_18k_gas.prm with the PID OFF)
// [Claude, 2026-09-21] GJK-only rod hopper WITH the 406 rods (identical to job 4252146: GJK/EPA contacts, no caps, rot-mass on, tightLayer1, sweep at |u|>0.17 + dense scan armed from 3000) but PID DISABLED with the fixed
// force accelerationXOverride 5.9e-7 taken from the no-clog reference 4252463. Fresh start, 18000 steps, VTK every 5000 (fluid crop z now 0..140). Only PIDParameters, the fluid crop z and this header differ from the 4252146 prm.
// hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidon_2node_gjk_sanity_18k_gas.prm   (copy of hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidon_2node_gjk_gas.prm, 18000 steps, + fluid sanity sweep)
// [Claude, 2026-09-20] GJK/EPA-only contacts, NO rod caps, useRotationalEffectiveMass true, useTightLayer1 true, collisionTimeFactor default (4), fresh start, 18000 steps, dense NaN scan + fluidSanity* sweep armed from step 3000.
// hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidon_2node_gjk_gas.prm   (GENERATED by hand from hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidon_2node_gas.prm; ONE line differs)
// [Claude, 2026-09-20] PRODUCTION RUN (60000 steps, PID on, 144 ranks) of the cylinder hopper with GJK/EPA ONLY (useAnalyticalContactDetection false): the analytic closed-form path aborted 3 of 3 fresh short runs
// (steps 5714, 3599, 3493, see THESIS_PLAN.md) while all three GJK-only short runs (6000 steps) were clean with rod-rod penetration <= 0.43 LU. Default stiffness (collisionTimeFactor 4). Checkpoints every 5000 steps.
// hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidon_2node_gas.prm   (GENERATED by gen_hopper_clog_cyl_prm.py -- edit the script, not this file)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// [Claude, 2026-09-19] "HOPPER" CLOGGING SETUP, CYLINDER VERSION (THESIS_PLAN.md item 3/4). NOT RUN YET.
// Companion of the sphere hopper (prms/hopper_clog_pidon_2node_frontblock_gas.prm, same channel/pillars/PID/probes/VTK): two cylindrical pillars centred on the
// Y walls (X=384, radius 12, central gap 16 LU, plan view "|) (|") -- but the debris are CYLINDERS, diameter:length = 1:3 (r=3, L=18; the sphere's
// 6 LU cross-section), LONG AXIS ALONG Y (across the channel), released together from a block pressed against the pillars.
//
// KEY GEOMETRIC FACT: the rod length 18 is LONGER than the 16 LU gap. A rod lying along Y therefore cannot pass the gap broadside: it has to rotate its axis towards the flow.
// Expect jamming of rods across the opening (log-jam like) rather than the free arching of the sphere hopper -- a different mechanism (rotation-limited passage).
//
// POPULATION: 406 rods = 2 across Y x 7 layers x 29 rows in X (pitch X/Y/Z = 7/20/7.52, >= 1 LU surface clearance rod-rod / wall / floor,
// checked exactly for parallel cylinders). Only 2 rods of length 18 fit across the 40 LU channel, and each rod is ~4.5x the volume of a sphere, hence far fewer than the 1015
// spheres (kept: the same 29 rows, i.e. the same block length). densityRatio {0.5,1.0,1.2} = 116/174/116, stratified by height like the sphere version (1.2 low, 1.0
// mid, 0.5 in the top two layers; the top layer's axis sits at the waterline Z=49.13, half submerged).
// Block X in [169.0,371.0], front row 1.04 LU (surface to pillar surface, exact rectangle-disc distance) from the pillar cylinders.
// All rods are held FIXED for 2000 steps (settlingSteps, no startInactive) and then released together; clearance >= 1 LU so [RELEASE-OVERLAP] cannot fire at release.
//
// CONTACT MODEL: useAnalyticalContactDetection true (Cylinder x Cylinder = analytical Kodam+Guo HYBRID, usePureAnalyticalCylinder false keeps the GJK/EPA fallback;
// Cylinder x pillar/wall analytic regardless) + useContactFilterOwnerTiebreak true; every experimental contact/buoyancy fix explicitly OFF (see ModelParameters) EXCEPT useRotationalEffectiveMass (ON, user request 2026-09-20: generalised effective mass incl. rotational inertia in the contact law) and useTightLayer1 (ON, user request 2026-09-20: the capsule/segment-distance pre-filter for Cylinder x Cylinder; near-parallel false-positive fix is in PaperAnalyticalContacts.h + an always-on capsule bound).
// Friction/restitution as in the sphere hopper (0.5 / 0.5).
//
// FLOW/UNITS: identical to the sphere hopper (PID on, target 0.04, water Z=49.13, Z=180 headroom, <768,40,180> / <64,20,30> = 144 ranks / 2 nodes).
// CAVEATS: the upstream clog probes (X=336) sit inside the rod block (unusable as a clog signal, as in the sphere case); the fluid VTK is cropped to X 128..640, Z 0..100
// (the rods are unfiltered); the [CylComputation] contact-path diagnostics make logs very large (the 100-floater sediment run's log was 594 MB) -- expect a big .out file.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 16, 12, 48 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 1, 0 >;
   loadSnapshot                  false;
   storeSnapshot                 false;
   snapshotFrequency             100000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <48, 36, 48>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 2.0;
   floorHeightFactor  2.249066;   // absoluteLiquidHeight = 16.003 + floor = 34.0 (water surface at z=34, bundle ~14 LU below it)
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
   targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0;      // still water
   proportionalGain            2e-4;
   derivativeGain              1e-6;
   integralGain                2e-4;
   maxRamp                     1e-4;
   minActuatingVariable        0;
   maxActuatingVariable        1e-3;
   enabled                     false;
   accelerationXOverride       1e-15;  // default 1e-15 = effectively no driving force
}

PhysicsParameters
{
   enableWetting     false;
   timesteps         16500;
   Re                3100;
   Fr                1.31;
   We                15.6188;
   useHardcodedUnits true;              // U = 0 (still water): fixed units, then overridden to the PRODUCTION values below
   relaxationRateOverride  1.99753;     // production omega (nu = 2.06502e-4)
   gravityOverride         5.82575e-05; // production gravity
   surfaceTensionOverride  0.00163945;  // production surface tension
   denseNanScanEnabled            true;
   denseNanScanFromStep           0;
   denseNanScanToStep             16500;
   highVelocityPrecursorThreshold 0.5;
   fluidSanityEnabled             true;
   fluidSanityFromStep            0;
   fluidSanityToStep              16500;
   fluidSanityEveryNSteps         1;
   fluidSanityMaxVelocity         0.17;
   fluidSanityDensityMin          0.1;
   fluidSanityDensityMax          1.9;
   fluidSanityMaxPopulation       2.0;
   fluidSanityFillTolerance       1.0;
   fluidSanityMaxExcessMass       1.0;
   fluidSanityMaxNeighbourVelocityJump 0.2;
   fluidSanityMaxNeighbourDensityJump  0.3;
   fluidSanityCheckTopology       true;
   fluidSanityStatsEveryNSteps    100;
   fluidSanityAbortAbove          0;
}

ParticleParameters
{
   inFileName spheres_out.dat;   // never opened -- see avgParticleDiameterOverride below
   bedCopiesInX 1;
   bedCopiesInY 1;
   avgParticleDiameterOverride 8.001943372119138;
   dxSIOverride                0.000362694127490625;
   densityRatio 2.55;
   fixingHeightFactor 1.5;
   frictionCoefficient 0.5;
   restitutionCoefficient 0.5;
   numSubCycles 10;
   useLubricationCorrection true;
   useNoSlipParticles false;
   useParticleBed false;
}

// (no pillars in this test)

FloatingCylinders
{
   FloatingCylinder { position < 15.1101, 11.7125, 23.5075 >; radius 3; length 18; axis < -0.742753, 0.652418, -0.150558 >; densityRatio 1; settlingSteps 0; }
   FloatingCylinder { position < 13.7250, 8.9561, 18.3963 >; radius 3; length 18; axis < -0.742753, 0.652418, -0.150558 >; densityRatio 1; settlingSteps 0; }
   FloatingCylinder { position < 17.6649, 13.4414, 18.3963 >; radius 3; length 18; axis < -0.742753, 0.652418, -0.150558 >; densityRatio 1; settlingSteps 0; }
}

ModelParameters
{
   useAnalyticalContactDetection false;   // GJK/EPA ONLY for all contacts (closed-form Kodam+Guo OFF; rod-vs-pillar also via GJK/EPA)
   usePureAnalyticalCylinder     false;  // (default, explicit) keep the GJK/EPA fallback for uncertain pairs
   useContactFilterOwnerTiebreak true;   // one rank accepts each boundary-straddling contact (min owner rank)

   // Experimental contact/buoyancy fixes: ALL explicitly OFF
   useTightTier1                 false;
   useTightLayer1                true;   // [Claude, 2026-09-20] ON by user request (capsule/segment-distance pre-filter for Cylinder x Cylinder, identical rejections to the always-on capsule bound but before the analytic dispatch)
   skipTier1                     false;
   useRoundedBoxCorners          false;
   useMultiPointBoxContact       false;
   useBoxOverlapCap              false;
   useAxisHysteresis             false;
   useContactManifold            false;
   useRotationalEffectiveMass    true;   // [Claude, 2026-09-20] ON for rods (user request): contact stiffness/damping from the generalised effective mass incl. rotational inertia at the contact point (exact for spheres, matters for rod rim/edge contacts)
   useSpheroBoxContact           false;
   useSpheroBoxAnalytical        false;
   useFraigeBoxContactModel      false;
   useFullVolumeAnalyticBuoyancy false;
   usePass3Reresolution          false;
   useAnalyticBoxBuoyancy        false;

   pdfReconstructionModel        OnlyMissing;
   pdfRefillingModel             EquilibriumRefilling;
   excessMassDistributionModel   EvenlyNewInterfaceFallbackLiquid;
   curvatureModel                FiniteDifferenceMethod;
   useSimpleMassExchange         false;
   cellConversionThreshold       1e-2;
   cellConversionForceThreshold  1e-1;
   useBognerReconstruction       true;
   useFillWeighting              true;
   useBognerThreePhaseMEM        true;
   useMemOnlyBuoyancy            true;
   rodPrescribedVelocityX        1e-09;    // TEST OPTION: rigid prescribed rod velocity (crash bundle: (-0.0096, 0.0043, 0.0062) at t=16300; z component dropped, the box is small)
   rodPrescribedVelocityY        0.0;
   rodPrescribedVelocityZ        0.0;
}

EvaluationParameters
{
   performanceLogFrequency 5000;
   evaluationFrequency     100;
   baseFolderName          eval;

   ClogMeasurement
   {
      upstreamPos       < 6, 18, 20 >;
      downstreamPos     < 42, 18, 20 >;
      probeHalfWidthXY  2;

      pillarUpstreamPos    < 6, 6, 20 >;
      pillarDownstreamPos  < 42, 6, 20 >;
   }
}

StabilityChecker
{
   checkFrequency 0;
   streamOutput   false;
   vtkOutput      true;
}

BoundaryParameters
{
   Border { direction T;  walldistance -1; NoSlip{} }
   Border { direction B;  walldistance -1; NoSlip{} }
}

MeshOutputParameters
{
   writeFrequency 0;
   baseFolder     mesh-out;
}

// 12 dumps over the run; fluid cropped to X 128..640, Z 0..100 (rods/pillars unfiltered).
VTK
{
   fluid_field
   {
      writeFrequency       500;
      ghostLayers          0;
      baseFolder           vtk-out;
      samplingResolution   1;
      useMPIIO false;

      writers
      {
         velocity;
         mapped_flag;
      }

      CellBB_filter_0 { min < 0, 0, 0 >;  max < 48, 36, 48 >; }

      inclusion_filters
      {
         CellBB_filter_0;
      }

      before_functions { gas_cell_zero_setter; }
   }

   domain_decomposition
   {
      writeFrequency             10000000000;
      baseFolder                 vtk-out;
      outputDomainDecomposition  true;
   }
}
